Corrected message:

Rebuild Layers panel object rows when their objects change

The check that decides whether a layer's object rows can be kept
instead of rebuilt compared rows against the layer's objects by raw
index, assuming every object has a row. Shapes and text set to
rasterize on finalize have none, so any such object shifted the
comparison. It also compared only the kind of object, so replacing one
text with another at the same position kept a row pointing at the old
one.

Rows are now compared against the same filtered object list used to
build them, and text and modifier rows must refer to the same object.
Shape rows are still matched by kind only: shape objects are recreated
on every save of the shape list, so an identity check would rebuild
every row on each mouse move while dragging.
